# Line endings, decided here rather than by whichever machine cloned the repo.
#
# This is not tidiness. `server/db/migrate.ts` checksums every migration so that
# editing an applied one stops the boot, and that checksum used to be taken over
# the bytes on disk. Git for Windows rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout, so the
# same commit produced different bytes on a Windows laptop and in a Linux
# container — and the first deploy that involved both refused to start, naming a
# migration nobody had touched.
#
# The checksum now normalises line endings, so that specific failure cannot
# recur. This file is the other half: it stops the working tree from diverging
# in the first place, for every tool that reads these files rather than only the
# one that was taught to cope.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit for the files where it has already cost something, and for the ones
# whose bytes are the point.
*.sql   text eol=lf
*.ts    text eol=lf
*.tsx   text eol=lf
*.js    text eol=lf
*.mjs   text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.toml  text eol=lf

# Binary, and never to be touched.
*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.docx  binary
